pursue each plotted course, in order. ref: $PURSUIT_ROUTE/1.courses.plot.yield.md

for the first plotted course that has not yet exited:

```sh
rhx education.pursuit.course init --course <slug>
rhx route.drive
```

`education.pursuit.course init` opens the course as its own route under
$PURSUIT_ROUTE/2.courses.pursue.yield/ and moves the bind to it. drive it to its last stone,
`6.exit`, which moves the bind back here. then pursue the next course.

once every plotted course has exited, pass this stone. its artifacts are the exits each course
wrote (`2.courses.pursue.yield/*/6.exit.yield.md`); no yield file of its own is owed:

```sh
rhx route.stone.set --stone 2.courses.pursue --as passed
```

one course at a time: course k reads the briefs course k−1 landed as given.
